#. Activity log summary for several messages that were deleted together when the channel was not recorded. {actor} is the member who deleted them, shown as a clickable user chip, or the word System. {count} is an ICU plural with the number of deleted messages, and # shows that number.
#: src/features/guild/utils/guild_tabs/audit_log/AuditLogExpressionMessageMessages.ts
msgid "{actor} deleted {count, plural, one {# message} other {# messages}}"
msgstr "{actor} heeft {count, plural, one {# bericht} other {# berichten}} verwijderd"

#. Activity log summary for several messages that were deleted together. {actor} is the member who deleted them, shown as a clickable user chip, or the word System. {count} is an ICU plural with the number of deleted messages, and # shows that number. {channel} is the channel the messages were in, shown as a channel name chip, or the deleted-channel label when the channel no longer exists.
#: src/features/guild/utils/guild_tabs/audit_log/AuditLogExpressionMessageMessages.ts
msgid "{actor} deleted {count, plural, one {# message} other {# messages}} in {channel}"
msgstr "{actor} heeft {count, plural, one {# bericht} other {# berichten}} verwijderd in {channel}"

#. Activity log summary for one message that was deleted when the channel was not recorded. {actor} is the member who deleted it, shown as a clickable user chip, or the word System.
#: src/features/guild/utils/guild_tabs/audit_log/AuditLogExpressionMessageMessages.ts
msgid "{actor} deleted a message"
msgstr "{actor} heeft een bericht verwijderd"

#. Activity log summary for one message that was deleted. {actor} is the member who deleted it, shown as a clickable user chip, or the word System. {channel} is the channel the message was in, shown as a channel name chip, or the deleted-channel label when the channel no longer exists.
#: src/features/guild/utils/guild_tabs/audit_log/AuditLogExpressionMessageMessages.ts
msgid "{actor} deleted a message in {channel}"
msgstr "{actor} heeft een bericht verwijderd in {channel}"

#. Activity log summary for a sticker that was deleted when its name was not recorded. {actor} is the member who deleted it, shown as a clickable user chip, or the word System.
#: src/features/guild/utils/guild_tabs/audit_log/AuditLogExpressionMessageMessages.ts
msgid "{actor} deleted a sticker"
msgstr "{actor} heeft een sticker verwijderd"

#. Activity log summary for a deleted webhook when its name was not recorded. {actor} is the member who deleted the webhook, shown as a clickable user chip, or the word System.
#: src/features/guild/utils/guild_tabs/audit_log/AuditLogInviteWebhookMessages.ts
msgid "{actor} deleted a webhook"
msgstr "{actor} heeft een webhook verwijderd"

#. Activity log summary for a custom emoji that was deleted when its name was not recorded. {actor} is the member who deleted it, shown as a clickable user chip, or the word System.
#: src/features/guild/utils/guild_tabs/audit_log/AuditLogExpressionMessageMessages.ts
msgid "{actor} deleted an emoji"
msgstr "{actor} heeft een emoji verwijderd"

#. Activity log summary for several messages that were deleted together when neither their number nor the channel was recorded. {actor} is the member who deleted them, shown as a clickable user chip, or the word System.
#: src/features/guild/utils/guild_tabs/audit_log/AuditLogExpressionMessageMessages.ts
msgid "{actor} deleted some messages"
msgstr "{actor} heeft enkele berichten verwijderd"

#. Activity log summary for several messages that were deleted together when their number was not recorded. {actor} is the member who deleted them, shown as a clickable user chip, or the word System. {channel} is the channel the messages were in, shown as a channel name chip, or the deleted-channel label when the channel no longer exists.
#: src/features/guild/utils/guild_tabs/audit_log/AuditLogExpressionMessageMessages.ts
msgid "{actor} deleted some messages in {channel}"
msgstr "{actor} heeft enkele berichten verwijderd in {channel}"

#. Activity log summary when an announcement channel was deleted. {actor} is the member who made the change, shown as a clickable user chip, or the word System. {channel} is the deleted channel, shown as a channel chip with the name it had.
#: src/features/guild/utils/guild_tabs/audit_log/AuditLogChannelMessages.ts
msgid "{actor} deleted the announcement channel {channel}"
msgstr "{actor} heeft het aankondigingskanaal {channel} verwijderd"

#. Activity log summary when a channel category was deleted. {actor} is the member who made the change, shown as a clickable user chip, or the word System. {channel} is the deleted category, shown as a channel chip with the name it had.
#: src/features/guild/utils/guild_tabs/audit_log/AuditLogChannelMessages.ts
msgid "{actor} deleted the category {channel}"
msgstr "{actor} heeft de categorie {channel} verwijderd"

#. Activity log summary when a channel of a type this app version cannot name was deleted. {actor} is the member who made the change, shown as a clickable user chip, or the word System. {channel} is the deleted channel, shown as a channel chip with the name it had.
#: src/features/guild/utils/guild_tabs/audit_log/AuditLogChannelMessages.ts
msgid "{actor} deleted the channel {channel}"
msgstr "{actor} heeft het kanaal {channel} verwijderd"

#. Activity log summary for a custom emoji that was deleted from the community. {actor} is the member who deleted it, shown as a clickable user chip, or the word System. {emoji} is the name of the deleted emoji between colons, for example :blobcat:, shown without an image.
#: src/features/guild/utils/guild_tabs/audit_log/AuditLogExpressionMessageMessages.ts
msgid "{actor} deleted the emoji {emoji}"
msgstr "{actor} heeft de emoji {emoji} verwijderd"

#. Activity log summary when a forum channel was deleted. {channel} is the deleted channel, shown as a channel chip with the name it had.
#: src/features/guild/utils/guild_tabs/audit_log/AuditLogForumPresentation.ts
msgid "{actor} deleted the forum channel {channel}"
msgstr "{actor} heeft het forumkanaal {channel} verwijderd"

#. Activity log summary for a deleted invite link when its channel was not recorded. {actor} is the member who deleted the invite, shown as a clickable user chip, or the word System. {code} is the invite code, shown as boxed text.
#: src/features/guild/utils/guild_tabs/audit_log/AuditLogInviteWebhookMessages.ts
msgid "{actor} deleted the invite {code}"
msgstr "{actor} heeft de uitnodiging {code} verwijderd"

#. Activity log summary for a deleted invite link. {actor} is the member who deleted the invite, shown as a clickable user chip, or the word System. {code} is the invite code, shown as boxed text. {channel} is the channel the invite led to, shown as a channel chip.
#: src/features/guild/utils/guild_tabs/audit_log/AuditLogInviteWebhookMessages.ts
msgid "{actor} deleted the invite {code} for {channel}"
msgstr "{actor} heeft de uitnodiging {code} voor {channel} verwijderd"

#. Activity log summary when a link channel was deleted. A link channel is a channel list entry that opens a web address. {actor} is the member who made the change, shown as a clickable user chip, or the word System. {channel} is the deleted channel, shown as a channel chip with the name it had.
#: src/features/guild/utils/guild_tabs/audit_log/AuditLogChannelMessages.ts
msgid "{actor} deleted the link channel {channel}"
msgstr "{actor} heeft het linkkanaal {channel} verwijderd"

#. Activity log summary when a media channel was deleted. {channel} is the deleted channel, shown as a channel chip with the name it had.
#: src/features/guild/utils/guild_tabs/audit_log/AuditLogForumPresentation.ts
msgid "{actor} deleted the media channel {channel}"
msgstr "{actor} heeft het mediakanaal {channel} verwijderd"

#. Activity log summary for a role that was deleted from the community. {actor} is the member who deleted it, shown as a clickable user chip, or the word System. {role} is the deleted role, shown in bold with the name it had when it was deleted, or deleted-role when that name was not recorded. The app adds the bold, so do not add ** or <b>. Use the same word for role as the rest of the app.
#: src/features/guild/utils/guild_tabs/audit_log/AuditLogRoleMessages.ts
msgid "{actor} deleted the role {role}"
msgstr "{actor} heeft de rol {role} verwijderd"

#. Activity log summary for a sticker that was deleted from the community. {actor} is the member who deleted it, shown as a clickable user chip, or the word System. {name} is the name of the deleted sticker, shown in bold. The app adds the bold, so do not add ** or <b>.
#: src/features/guild/utils/guild_tabs/audit_log/AuditLogExpressionMessageMessages.ts
msgid "{actor} deleted the sticker {name}"
msgstr "{actor} heeft de sticker {name} verwijderd"

#. Activity log summary when a text channel was deleted. {actor} is the member who made the change, shown as a clickable user chip, or the word System. {channel} is the deleted channel, shown as a channel chip with the name it had.
#: src/features/guild/utils/guild_tabs/audit_log/AuditLogChannelMessages.ts
msgid "{actor} deleted the text channel {channel}"
msgstr "{actor} heeft het tekstkanaal {channel} verwijderd"

#. Activity log summary when a thread was deleted. {actor} is the member who made the change, shown as a clickable user chip, or the word System. {channel} is the thread, shown as a channel chip with its recorded name.
#: src/features/guild/utils/guild_tabs/audit_log/AuditLogThreadPresentation.ts
msgid "{actor} deleted the thread {channel}"
msgstr "{actor} heeft de thread {channel} verwijderd"

#. Activity log summary when a voice channel was deleted. {actor} is the member who made the change, shown as a clickable user chip, or the word System. {channel} is the deleted channel, shown as a channel chip with the name it had.
#: src/features/guild/utils/guild_tabs/audit_log/AuditLogChannelMessages.ts
msgid "{actor} deleted the voice channel {channel}"
msgstr "{actor} heeft het spraakkanaal {channel} verwijderd"

#. Activity log summary for a deleted webhook when its channel was not recorded. {actor} is the member who deleted the webhook, shown as a clickable user chip, or the word System. {name} is the name the webhook had, shown in bold by the app. Do not add ** or <b> around it.
#: src/features/guild/utils/guild_tabs/audit_log/AuditLogInviteWebhookMessages.ts
msgid "{actor} deleted the webhook {name}"
msgstr "{actor} heeft de webhook {name} verwijderd"

#. Activity log summary for a deleted webhook. {actor} is the member who deleted the webhook, shown as a clickable user chip, or the word System. {name} is the name the webhook had, shown in bold by the app. Do not add ** or <b> around it. {channel} is the channel the webhook posted in, shown as a channel chip.
#: src/features/guild/utils/guild_tabs/audit_log/AuditLogInviteWebhookMessages.ts
msgid "{actor} deleted the webhook {name} from {channel}"
msgstr "{actor} heeft de webhook {name} uit {channel} verwijderd"

#. Activity log summary for a member who was removed from a voice channel by someone else. {actor} is the member who disconnected them, shown as a clickable user chip, or the word System. {target} is the member who was disconnected, shown as a clickable user chip. {channel} is the voice channel they were in, shown as a channel chip with the channel name.
#: src/features/guild/utils/guild_tabs/audit_log/AuditLogMemberMessages.ts
msgid "{actor} disconnected {target} from {channel}"
msgstr "{actor} heeft de verbinding van {target} met {channel} verbroken"

#. Activity log summary for a member who was removed from a voice channel by someone else when the channel was not recorded. {actor} is the member who disconnected them, shown as a clickable user chip, or the word System. {target} is the member who was disconnected, shown as a clickable user chip.
#: src/features/guild/utils/guild_tabs/audit_log/AuditLogMemberMessages.ts
msgid "{actor} disconnected {target} from voice"
msgstr "{actor} heeft de verbinding van {target} met spraakchat verbroken"

#. Activity log summary for a member who removed themselves from a voice channel using moderator tools. {actor} is that member, shown as a clickable user chip. {channel} is the voice channel they left, shown as a channel chip with the channel name.
#: src/features/guild/utils/guild_tabs/audit_log/AuditLogMemberMessages.ts
msgid "{actor} disconnected from {channel}"
msgstr "{actor} heeft de verbinding met {channel} verbroken"

#. Activity log summary for a member who removed themselves from a voice channel using moderator tools, when the channel was not recorded. {actor} is that member, shown as a clickable user chip.
#: src/features/guild/utils/guild_tabs/audit_log/AuditLogMemberMessages.ts
msgid "{actor} disconnected from voice"
msgstr "{actor} heeft de verbinding met spraakchat verbroken"

#. Activity log summary when a member followed an announcement channel, so messages published there are now copied into a channel of this community. {actor} is the member who followed it, shown as a clickable user chip, or the word System. {channel} is the channel in this community that receives the copies, shown as a channel chip.
#: src/features/guild/utils/guild_tabs/audit_log/AuditLogInviteWebhookMessages.ts
msgid "{actor} followed an announcement channel into {channel}"
msgstr "{actor} heeft een aankondigingskanaal gevolgd naar {channel}"

#. Activity log summary for a role that was given to a member. {actor} is the member who gave the role, shown as a clickable user chip, or the word System. {target} is the member who got the role, shown as a clickable user chip. {role} is the role, shown as a role chip with its name.
#: src/features/guild/utils/guild_tabs/audit_log/AuditLogMemberMessages.ts
msgid "{actor} gave {target} the role {role}"
msgstr "{actor} heeft {target} de rol {role} gegeven"

#. Activity log summary for a member who was kicked from the community. {actor} is the member who kicked them, shown as a clickable user chip, or the word System. {target} is the member who was kicked, shown as a clickable user chip.
#: src/features/guild/utils/guild_tabs/audit_log/AuditLogMemberMessages.ts
msgid "{actor} kicked {target}"
msgstr "{actor} heeft {target} uit de community verwijderd"

#. Activity log summary for a moderator who let a member hear the voice channels of this community again. This is about what the member hears and not about the microphone of the member, so it must read clearly differently from the row where a moderator turns the microphone back on. Describe the effect the way the English does. Do not name the action with a noun such as a community deafen. This is a past tense record of an action that already happened, never an instruction to the reader. {actor} is the member who lifted it, shown as a clickable user chip, or the word System. {target} is the member who can hear others again, shown as a clickable user chip.
#: src/features/guild/utils/guild_tabs/audit_log/AuditLogMemberMessages.ts
msgid "{actor} let {target} hear others in this community again"
msgstr "{actor} heeft ervoor gezorgd dat {target} anderen in deze community weer hoort"

#. Activity log summary for a kind of change this app version cannot describe, usually because the server is newer than the app. {actor} is the member who made the change, shown as a clickable user chip, or the word System.
#: src/features/guild/utils/guild_tabs/audit_log/AuditLogSharedMessages.ts
msgid "{actor} made a change that this version of the app cannot show"
msgstr "{actor} heeft een wijziging aangebracht die deze versie van de app niet kan weergeven"

#. Activity log summary for a member who was moved from one voice channel to another. {actor} is the member who did the move, shown as a clickable user chip, or the word System. {target} is the member who was moved, shown as a clickable user chip. {oldChannel} is the voice channel they were in and {newChannel} is the voice channel they were moved to, both shown as channel chips with the channel name.
#: src/features/guild/utils/guild_tabs/audit_log/AuditLogMemberMessages.ts
msgid "{actor} moved {target} from {oldChannel} to {newChannel}"
msgstr "{actor} heeft {target} verplaatst van {oldChannel} naar {newChannel}"

#. Activity log summary for a member who was moved to a voice channel when the channel they came from was not recorded. {actor} is the member who did the move, shown as a clickable user chip, or the word System. {target} is the member who was moved, shown as a clickable user chip. {channel} is the voice channel they were moved to, shown as a channel chip with the channel name.
#: src/features/guild/utils/guild_tabs/audit_log/AuditLogMemberMessages.ts
msgid "{actor} moved {target} to {channel}"
msgstr "{actor} heeft {target} verplaatst naar {channel}"

#. Activity log summary for a member who was moved to another voice channel when the channel they were moved to was not recorded. {actor} is the member who did the move, shown as a clickable user chip, or the word System. {target} is the member who was moved, shown as a clickable user chip.
#: src/features/guild/utils/guild_tabs/audit_log/AuditLogMemberMessages.ts
msgid "{actor} moved {target} to a different voice channel"
msgstr "{actor} heeft {target} naar een ander spraakkanaal verplaatst"

#. Activity log summary for a member who moved themselves from one voice channel to another using moderator tools. {actor} is that member, shown as a clickable user chip. {oldChannel} is the voice channel they were in and {newChannel} is the voice channel they moved to, both shown as channel chips with the channel name.
#: src/features/guild/utils/guild_tabs/audit_log/AuditLogMemberMessages.ts
msgid "{actor} moved from {oldChannel} to {newChannel}"
msgstr "{actor} heeft zichzelf verplaatst van {oldChannel} naar {newChannel}"

#. Activity log summary for a role whose group of members was moved lower in the member list. {actor} is the member who moved it, shown as a clickable user chip, or the word System. {role} is the role, shown in bold with its name, or deleted-role when its name is unknown. The app adds the bold, so do not add ** or <b>. Use the same word for role as the rest of the app.
#: src/features/guild/utils/guild_tabs/audit_log/AuditLogRoleMessages.ts
msgid "{actor} moved the role {role} down in the member list"
msgstr "{actor} heeft de rol {role} lager geplaatst in de ledenlijst"

#. Activity log summary for a role that was moved lower in the community role list, where higher roles rank above lower ones. {actor} is the member who moved it, shown as a clickable user chip, or the word System. {role} is the role that moved, shown in bold with its name, @everyone for the default role every member has, or deleted-role when its name is unknown. The app adds the bold, so do not add ** or <b>. Use the same word for role as the rest of the app.
#: src/features/guild/utils/guild_tabs/audit_log/AuditLogRoleMessages.ts
msgid "{actor} moved the role {role} down in the role list"
msgstr "{actor} heeft de rol {role} lager geplaatst in de rollenlijst"

#. Activity log summary for a role whose group of members was moved higher in the member list. {actor} is the member who moved it, shown as a clickable user chip, or the word System. {role} is the role, shown in bold with its name, or deleted-role when its name is unknown. The app adds the bold, so do not add ** or <b>. Use the same word for role as the rest of the app.
#: src/features/guild/utils/guild_tabs/audit_log/AuditLogRoleMessages.ts
msgid "{actor} moved the role {role} up in the member list"
msgstr "{actor} heeft de rol {role} hoger geplaatst in de ledenlijst"

#. Activity log summary for a role that was moved higher in the community role list, where higher roles rank above lower ones. {actor} is the member who moved it, shown as a clickable user chip, or the word System. {role} is the role that moved, shown in bold with its name, @everyone for the default role every member has, or deleted-role when its name is unknown. The app adds the bold, so do not add ** or <b>. Use the same word for role as the rest of the app.
#: src/features/guild/utils/guild_tabs/audit_log/AuditLogRoleMessages.ts
msgid "{actor} moved the role {role} up in the role list"
msgstr "{actor} heeft de rol {role} hoger geplaatst in de rollenlijst"

#. Activity log summary for a member who moved themselves to a voice channel using moderator tools, when the channel they came from was not recorded. {actor} is that member, shown as a clickable user chip. {channel} is the voice channel they moved to, shown as a channel chip with the channel name.
#: src/features/guild/utils/guild_tabs/audit_log/AuditLogMemberMessages.ts
msgid "{actor} moved to {channel}"
msgstr "{actor} heeft zichzelf naar {channel} verplaatst"

#. Activity log summary for a member who moved themselves to another voice channel using moderator tools, when the channel they moved to was not recorded. {actor} is that member, shown as a clickable user chip.
#: src/features/guild/utils/guild_tabs/audit_log/AuditLogMemberMessages.ts
msgid "{actor} moved to a different voice channel"
msgstr "{actor} heeft zichzelf naar een ander spraakkanaal verplaatst"

#. Activity log summary when a member paused invites. Pausing invites disables every invite link of the community, so nobody new can join through one until invites are enabled again. Existing members are not affected. Use the same verb as the Pause invites button. {actor} is the member who made the change, shown as a clickable user chip, or the word System.
#: src/features/guild/utils/guild_tabs/audit_log/AuditLogGuildMessages.ts
msgid "{actor} paused invites"
msgstr "{actor} heeft uitnodigingen gepauzeerd"

#. Activity log summary for a message that was pinned when the channel was not recorded. Pinned means the message was added to the pinned messages of its channel. {actor} is the member who pinned it, shown as a clickable user chip, or the word System.
#: src/features/guild/utils/guild_tabs/audit_log/AuditLogExpressionMessageMessages.ts
msgid "{actor} pinned a message"
msgstr "{actor} heeft een bericht vastgezet"

#. Activity log summary for a message that was pinned. Pinned means the message was added to the pinned messages of the channel. {actor} is the member who pinned it, shown as a clickable user chip, or the word System. {channel} is the channel the message is in, shown as a channel name chip, or the deleted-channel label when the channel no longer exists.
#: src/features/guild/utils/guild_tabs/audit_log/AuditLogExpressionMessageMessages.ts
msgid "{actor} pinned a message in {channel}"
msgstr "{actor} heeft een bericht vastgezet in {channel}"

#. Activity log summary for inactive members who were removed from the community in one go. {actor} is the member who started the prune, shown as a clickable user chip, or the word System.
#: src/features/guild/utils/guild_tabs/audit_log/AuditLogMemberMessages.ts
msgid "{actor} pruned inactive members"
msgstr "{actor} heeft inactieve leden verwijderd"

#. Activity log summary for a nickname that someone removed from another member in the community. {actor} is the member who removed the nickname, shown as a clickable user chip, or the word System. {nick} is the nickname that was removed. The app shows it in bold, so do not add ** or <b>. {target} is the member who lost the nickname, shown as a clickable user chip.
#: src/features/guild/utils/guild_tabs/audit_log/AuditLogMemberMessages.ts
msgid "{actor} removed the nickname {nick} from {target}"
msgstr "{actor} heeft de bijnaam {nick} van {target} verwijderd"

#. Activity log summary when the permission override for one member was removed from a channel, so the member has their usual permissions there again. A permission override is a channel-level exception to the permissions of a role or member. It allows or denies chosen permissions in one channel or category only. Use the same word for override as the channel permissions settings, such as Add override. {actor} is the member who made the change, shown as a clickable user chip, or the word System. {user} is the member the override applied to, shown as a clickable user chip. {channel} is the channel, shown as a channel chip with its name.
#: src/features/guild/utils/guild_tabs/audit_log/AuditLogChannelMessages.ts
msgid "{actor} removed the permission override for {user} from {channel}"
msgstr "{actor} heeft de aangepaste toegangsrechten voor {user} uit {channel} verwijderd"

#. Activity log summary when the permission override for every member of the community was removed from a channel. A permission override is a channel-level exception to the permissions of a role or member. It allows or denies chosen permissions in one channel or category only. Use the same word for override as the channel permissions settings, such as Add override. Keep @everyone unchanged. It is the name of the role that includes all members. {actor} is the member who made the change, shown as a clickable user chip, or the word System. {channel} is the channel, shown as a channel chip with its name.
#: src/features/guild/utils/guild_tabs/audit_log/AuditLogChannelMessages.ts
msgid "{actor} removed the permission override for @everyone from {channel}"
msgstr "{actor} heeft de aangepaste toegangsrechten voor @everyone uit {channel} verwijderd"

#. Activity log summary when the permission override for a role was removed from a channel, so the role has its usual permissions there again. A permission override is a channel-level exception to the permissions of a role or member. It allows or denies chosen permissions in one channel or category only. Use the same word for override as the channel permissions settings, such as Add override. {actor} is the member who made the change, shown as a clickable user chip, or the word System. {role} is the role, shown as a role chip with its name. {channel} is the channel, shown as a channel chip with its name.
#: src/features/guild/utils/guild_tabs/audit_log/AuditLogChannelMessages.ts
msgid "{actor} removed the permission override for the role {role} from {channel}"
msgstr "{actor} heeft de aangepaste toegangsrechten voor de rol {role} uit {channel} verwijderd"

#. Activity log summary for a role that was taken away from a member. {actor} is the member who removed the role, shown as a clickable user chip, or the word System. {role} is the role, shown as a role chip with its name. {target} is the member who lost the role, shown as a clickable user chip.
#: src/features/guild/utils/guild_tabs/audit_log/AuditLogMemberMessages.ts
msgid "{actor} removed the role {role} from {target}"
msgstr "{actor} heeft de rol {role} van {target} verwijderd"

#. Activity log summary for a timeout that was ended early. A timeout is the moderation action that stops a member from sending messages, reacting and joining voice until it ends. It is not a ban, a kick or a community mute. {actor} is the member who removed the timeout, shown as a clickable user chip, or the word System. {target} is the member whose timeout was removed, shown as a clickable user chip.
#: src/features/guild/utils/guild_tabs/audit_log/AuditLogMemberMessages.ts
msgid "{actor} removed the timeout for {target}"
msgstr "{actor} heeft de time-out voor {target} verwijderd"

#. Activity log summary when a member removed the vanity URL, the custom invite link of the community. {actor} is the member who made the change, shown as a clickable user chip, or the word System. {code} is the vanity URL code that was removed, shown as boxed text.
#: src/features/guild/utils/guild_tabs/audit_log/AuditLogGuildMessages.ts
msgid "{actor} removed the vanity URL {code}"
msgstr "{actor} heeft de aangepaste URL {code} verwijderd"

#. Activity log summary for a member who removed the accent color from their community profile. A community profile is the profile a member uses only in this community, in place of their global profile. The accent color belongs to the member, not to the community. "Their" means the same member as {actor}. {actor} is that member, shown as a clickable user chip.
#: src/features/guild/utils/guild_tabs/audit_log/AuditLogMemberMessages.ts
msgid "{actor} removed their community profile accent color"
msgstr "{actor} heeft de accentkleur van hun communityprofiel verwijderd"

#. Activity log summary for a member who removed the avatar from their community profile. A community profile is the profile a member uses only in this community, in place of their global profile. The avatar belongs to the member, not to the community. "Their" means the same member as {actor}. {actor} is that member, shown as a clickable user chip.
#: src/features/guild/utils/guild_tabs/audit_log/AuditLogMemberMessages.ts
msgid "{actor} removed their community profile avatar"
msgstr "{actor} heeft hun communityprofielavatar verwijderd"

#. Activity log summary for a member who removed the banner image from their community profile. A community profile is the profile a member uses only in this community, in place of their global profile. The banner belongs to the member, not to the community. "Their" means the same member as {actor}. {actor} is that member, shown as a clickable user chip.
#: src/features/guild/utils/guild_tabs/audit_log/AuditLogMemberMessages.ts
msgid "{actor} removed their community profile banner"
msgstr "{actor} heeft hun communityprofielbanner verwijderd"

#. Activity log summary for a member who removed the bio from their community profile. A community profile is the profile a member uses only in this community, in place of their global profile. The bio belongs to the member, not to the community. "Their" means the same member as {actor}. {actor} is that member, shown as a clickable user chip.
#: src/features/guild/utils/guild_tabs/audit_log/AuditLogMemberMessages.ts
msgid "{actor} removed their community profile bio"
msgstr "{actor} heeft de bio van hun communityprofiel verwijderd"

#. Activity log summary for a member who removed the pronouns from their community profile. Pronouns are the words the member wants others to use for them, such as they/them. A community profile is the profile a member uses only in this community, in place of their global profile. The pronouns belong to the member, not to the community. "Their" means the same member as {actor}. {actor} is that member, shown as a clickable user chip.
#: src/features/guild/utils/guild_tabs/audit_log/AuditLogMemberMessages.ts
msgid "{actor} removed their community profile pronouns"
msgstr "{actor} heeft de voornaamwoorden van hun communityprofiel verwijderd"

#. Activity log summary for a member who removed their own nickname in the community. "Their" means the same member as {actor}. {actor} is that member, shown as a clickable user chip. {nick} is the nickname that was removed. The app shows it in bold, so do not add ** or <b>.
#: src/features/guild/utils/guild_tabs/audit_log/AuditLogMemberMessages.ts
msgid "{actor} removed their nickname {nick}"
msgstr "{actor} heeft hun bijnaam {nick} verwijderd"

#. Activity log summary when the only change to an announcement channel was its name. {actor} is the member who made the change, shown as a clickable user chip, or the word System. {oldName} is the name before the change and {newName} the name after, both shown in bold. The app adds the bold, so do not add ** or <b>.
#: src/features/guild/utils/guild_tabs/audit_log/AuditLogChannelMessages.ts
msgid "{actor} renamed the announcement channel {oldName} to {newName}"
msgstr "{actor} heeft het aankondigingskanaal {oldName} hernoemd naar {newName}"

#. Activity log summary when the only change to a channel category was its name. {actor} is the member who made the change, shown as a clickable user chip, or the word System. {oldName} is the name before the change and {newName} the name after, both shown in bold. The app adds the bold, so do not add ** or <b>.
#: src/features/guild/utils/guild_tabs/audit_log/AuditLogChannelMessages.ts
msgid "{actor} renamed the category {oldName} to {newName}"
msgstr "{actor} heeft de categorie {oldName} hernoemd naar {newName}"

#. Activity log summary when the only change to a channel of a type this app version cannot name was its name. {actor} is the member who made the change, shown as a clickable user chip, or the word System. {oldName} is the name before the change and {newName} the name after, both shown in bold. The app adds the bold, so do not add ** or <b>.
#: src/features/guild/utils/guild_tabs/audit_log/AuditLogChannelMessages.ts
msgid "{actor} renamed the channel {oldName} to {newName}"
msgstr "{actor} heeft het kanaal {oldName} hernoemd naar {newName}"

#. Activity log summary when the only community setting a member changed was the community name. {actor} is the member who made the change, shown as a clickable user chip, or the word System. {oldName} is the previous community name and {newName} is the new community name, both shown in bold. The app adds the bold, so do not add ** or <b>.
#: src/features/guild/utils/guild_tabs/audit_log/AuditLogGuildMessages.ts
msgid "{actor} renamed the community from {oldName} to {newName}"
msgstr "{actor} heeft de community hernoemd van {oldName} naar {newName}"

#. Activity log summary for a custom emoji that got a new name. Only the name changed. The emoji was not replaced with a different one. {actor} is the member who renamed it, shown as a clickable user chip, or the word System. {oldEmoji} is the previous name between colons, shown without an image. {newEmoji} is the new name between colons, shown after the emoji image when the emoji still exists.
#: src/features/guild/utils/guild_tabs/audit_log/AuditLogExpressionMessageMessages.ts
msgid "{actor} renamed the emoji {oldEmoji} to {newEmoji}"
msgstr "{actor} heeft de emoji {oldEmoji} hernoemd naar {newEmoji}"

#. Activity log summary when the only change to a forum channel was its name. {oldName} and {newName} are shown in bold by the app, so do not add ** or <b>.
#: src/features/guild/utils/guild_tabs/audit_log/AuditLogForumPresentation.ts
msgid "{actor} renamed the forum channel {oldName} to {newName}"
msgstr "{actor} heeft het forumkanaal {oldName} hernoemd naar {newName}"

#. Activity log summary when the only change to a link channel was its name. A link channel is a channel list entry that opens a web address. {actor} is the member who made the change, shown as a clickable user chip, or the word System. {oldName} is the name before the change and {newName} the name after, both shown in bold. The app adds the bold, so do not add ** or <b>.
#: src/features/guild/utils/guild_tabs/audit_log/AuditLogChannelMessages.ts
msgid "{actor} renamed the link channel {oldName} to {newName}"
msgstr "{actor} heeft het linkkanaal {oldName} hernoemd naar {newName}"

#. Activity log summary when the only change to a media channel was its name. {oldName} and {newName} are shown in bold by the app, so do not add ** or <b>.
#: src/features/guild/utils/guild_tabs/audit_log/AuditLogForumPresentation.ts
msgid "{actor} renamed the media channel {oldName} to {newName}"
msgstr "{actor} heeft het mediakanaal {oldName} hernoemd naar {newName}"

#. Activity log summary for a role that got a new name and no other change. {actor} is the member who renamed it, shown as a clickable user chip, or the word System. {oldName} is the role name before the change and {newName} is the role name after it. Do not swap them. The app shows both in bold, so do not add ** or <b> around them. Use the same word for role as the rest of the app.
#: src/features/guild/utils/guild_tabs/audit_log/AuditLogRoleMessages.ts
msgid "{actor} renamed the role {oldName} to {newName}"
msgstr "{actor} heeft de rol {oldName} hernoemd naar {newName}"

#. Activity log summary for a sticker that got a new name and no other change. Only the name changed. The sticker was not replaced with a different one. {actor} is the member who renamed it, shown as a clickable user chip, or the word System. {oldName} is the previous sticker name and {newName} is the new one, both shown in bold. The app adds the bold, so do not add ** or <b>.
#: src/features/guild/utils/guild_tabs/audit_log/AuditLogExpressionMessageMessages.ts
msgid "{actor} renamed the sticker {oldName} to {newName}"
msgstr "{actor} heeft de sticker {oldName} hernoemd naar {newName}"

#. Activity log summary when the only change to a text channel was its name. {actor} is the member who made the change, shown as a clickable user chip, or the word System. {oldName} is the name before the change and {newName} the name after, both shown in bold. The app adds the bold, so do not add ** or <b>.
#: src/features/guild/utils/guild_tabs/audit_log/AuditLogChannelMessages.ts
msgid "{actor} renamed the text channel {oldName} to {newName}"
msgstr "{actor} heeft het tekstkanaal {oldName} hernoemd naar {newName}"

#. Activity log summary when the only change to a voice channel was its name. {actor} is the member who made the change, shown as a clickable user chip, or the word System. {oldName} is the name before the change and {newName} the name after, both shown in bold. The app adds the bold, so do not add ** or <b>.
#: src/features/guild/utils/guild_tabs/audit_log/AuditLogChannelMessages.ts
msgid "{actor} renamed the voice channel {oldName} to {newName}"
msgstr "{actor} heeft het spraakkanaal {oldName} hernoemd naar {newName}"

#. Activity log summary for a webhook whose name was the only thing changed. {actor} is the member who renamed the webhook, shown as a clickable user chip, or the word System. {oldName} is the previous name of the webhook and {newName} is its new name, both shown in bold by the app. Do not add ** or <b> around them.
#: src/features/guild/utils/guild_tabs/audit_log/AuditLogInviteWebhookMessages.ts
msgid "{actor} renamed the webhook {oldName} to {newName}"
msgstr "{actor} heeft de webhook {oldName} hernoemd naar {newName}"

#. Activity log summary for a role that lost its own place in the order of role groups in the member list, so that order follows the role list again. Reset means the position went back to the default. The member list position is where the group of members with this role appears in the member list. It is not a position of the member list itself. {actor} is the member who reset it, shown as a clickable user chip, or the word System. {role} is the role, shown in bold with its name, or deleted-role when its name is unknown. The app adds the bold, so do not add ** or <b>. Use the same word for role as the rest of the app.
#: src/features/guild/utils/guild_tabs/audit_log/AuditLogRoleMessages.ts
msgid "{actor} reset the member list position for the role {role}"
msgstr "{actor} heeft de positie in de ledenlijst voor de rol {role} gereset"

#. Activity log summary when a member resumed invites after they were paused. Resuming invites enables the invite links of the community again, so people can join through them. It is the reverse of pausing invites and matches the Enable invites button. It does not mean invites were repeated or sent again. {actor} is the member who made the change, shown as a clickable user chip, or the word System.
#: src/features/guild/utils/guild_tabs/audit_log/AuditLogGuildMessages.ts
msgid "{actor} resumed invites"
msgstr "{actor} heeft uitnodigingen hervat"

#. Activity log summary for a role that was given its own place in the order of role groups in the member list. Until then that order followed the role list. The member list position is where the group of members with this role appears in the member list. It is not a position of the member list itself. {actor} is the member who set it, shown as a clickable user chip, or the word System. {role} is the role, shown in bold with its name, or deleted-role when its name is unknown. The app adds the bold, so do not add ** or <b>. Use the same word for role as the rest of the app.
#: src/features/guild/utils/guild_tabs/audit_log/AuditLogRoleMessages.ts
msgid "{actor} set a member list position for the role {role}"
msgstr "{actor} heeft een positie in de ledenlijst ingesteld voor de rol {role}"

#. Activity log summary for a nickname that someone gave to another member who had no nickname in the community. {actor} is the member who set the nickname, shown as a clickable user chip, or the word System. {target} is the member who got the nickname, shown as a clickable user chip. {nick} is the new nickname. The app shows it in bold, so do not add ** or <b>.
#: src/features/guild/utils/guild_tabs/audit_log/AuditLogMemberMessages.ts
msgid "{actor} set the nickname of {target} to {nick}"
msgstr "{actor} heeft de bijnaam van {target} ingesteld op {nick}"

#. Activity log summary when a member gave the community a vanity URL, the custom invite link of the community, when it had none. {actor} is the member who made the change, shown as a clickable user chip, or the word System. {code} is the new vanity URL code, shown as boxed text.
#: src/features/guild/utils/guild_tabs/audit_log/AuditLogGuildMessages.ts
msgid "{actor} set the vanity URL to {code}"
msgstr "{actor} heeft de aangepaste URL ingesteld op {code}"

#. Activity log summary for a member who added or changed the accent color on their community profile. A community profile is the profile a member uses only in this community, in place of their global profile. The accent color belongs to the member, not to the community. "Their" means the same member as {actor}. {actor} is that member, shown as a clickable user chip. {color} is the new color as a hex code such as #FF0000, shown next to a dot in that color.
#: src/features/guild/utils/guild_tabs/audit_log/AuditLogMemberMessages.ts
msgid "{actor} set their community profile accent color to {color}"
msgstr "{actor} heeft de accentkleur van hun communityprofiel ingesteld op {color}"

#. Activity log summary for a member who added an avatar to their community profile. A community profile is the profile a member uses only in this community, in place of their global profile. The avatar belongs to the member, not to the community. {actor} is that member, shown as a clickable user chip.
#: src/features/guild/utils/guild_tabs/audit_log/AuditLogMemberMessages.ts
msgid "{actor} set their community profile avatar"
msgstr "{actor} heeft hun communityprofielavatar ingesteld"

#. Activity log summary for a member who added a banner image to their community profile. A community profile is the profile a member uses only in this community, in place of their global profile. The banner belongs to the member, not to the community. {actor} is that member, shown as a clickable user chip.
#: src/features/guild/utils/guild_tabs/audit_log/AuditLogMemberMessages.ts
msgid "{actor} set their community profile banner"
msgstr "{actor} heeft de banner van hun communityprofiel ingesteld"

#. Activity log summary for a member who added a bio to their community profile. A community profile is the profile a member uses only in this community, in place of their global profile. The bio belongs to the member, not to the community. "Their" means the same member as {actor}. {actor} is that member, shown as a clickable user chip. {text} is the new bio, shown as boxed text and shortened when long.
#: src/features/guild/utils/guild_tabs/audit_log/AuditLogMemberMessages.ts
msgid "{actor} set their community profile bio to {text}"
msgstr "{actor} heeft de bio van hun communityprofiel ingesteld op {text}"

#. Activity log summary for a member who added or changed the pronouns on their community profile. Pronouns are the words the member wants others to use for them, such as they/them. A community profile is the profile a member uses only in this community, in place of their global profile. The pronouns belong to the member, not to the community. "Their" means the same member as {actor}. {actor} is that member, shown as a clickable user chip. {text} is the new pronouns as the member wrote them, shown as boxed text.
#: src/features/guild/utils/guild_tabs/audit_log/AuditLogMemberMessages.ts
msgid "{actor} set their community profile pronouns to {text}"
msgstr "{actor} heeft de voornaamwoorden van hun communityprofiel ingesteld op {text}"

#. Activity log summary for a member who gave themselves a nickname in the community. "Their" means the same member as {actor}. {actor} is that member, shown as a clickable user chip. {nick} is the new nickname. The app shows it in bold, so do not add ** or <b>.
#: src/features/guild/utils/guild_tabs/audit_log/AuditLogMemberMessages.ts
msgid "{actor} set their nickname to {nick}"
msgstr "{actor} heeft hun bijnaam ingesteld op {nick}"

#. Activity log summary when a thread was created. {actor} is the member who made the change, shown as a clickable user chip, or the word System. {channel} is the thread, shown as a channel chip with its name.
#: src/features/guild/utils/guild_tabs/audit_log/AuditLogThreadPresentation.ts
msgid "{actor} started the thread {channel}"
msgstr "{actor} startte de thread {channel}"

#. Activity log summary for a moderator who stopped a member from hearing anyone in the voice channels of this community until it is undone. This is about what the member hears and not about the microphone of the member, so it must read clearly differently from the row where a moderator turns the microphone off. Describe the effect the way the English does. Do not name the action with a noun such as a community deafen. This is a past tense record of an action that already happened, never an instruction to the reader. {actor} is the member who stopped it, shown as a clickable user chip, or the word System. {target} is the member who can no longer hear others, shown as a clickable user chip.
#: src/features/guild/utils/guild_tabs/audit_log/AuditLogMemberMessages.ts
msgid "{actor} stopped {target} from hearing others in this community"
msgstr "{actor} heeft ervoor gezorgd dat {target} anderen in deze community niet meer hoort"

#. Activity log summary when a member removed a followed announcement channel, so its published messages are no longer copied into a channel of this community. {actor} is the member who removed it, shown as a clickable user chip, or the word System. {channel} is the channel in this community that received the copies, shown as a channel chip.
#: src/features/guild/utils/guild_tabs/audit_log/AuditLogInviteWebhookMessages.ts
msgid "{actor} stopped following an announcement channel in {channel}"
msgstr "{actor} is gestopt met het volgen van een aankondigingskanaal in {channel}"

#. Activity log summary for a member who was given a timeout. A timeout is the moderation action that stops a member from sending messages, reacting and joining voice until it ends. It is not a ban, a kick or a community mute. Use the same term as the "Timeout" and "Time out members" labels. {actor} is the member who gave the timeout, shown as a clickable user chip, or the word System. {target} is the member in timeout, shown as a clickable user chip. {date} is when the timeout ends, shown as a formatted date and time.
#: src/features/guild/utils/guild_tabs/audit_log/AuditLogMemberMessages.ts
msgid "{actor} timed out {target} until {date}"
msgstr "{actor} heeft {target} een time-out gegeven tot {date}"

#. Activity log summary when the community owner made another member the owner of the community. {actor} is the member who made the change, shown as a clickable user chip, or the word System. {user} is the new owner, shown as a clickable user chip.
#: src/features/guild/utils/guild_tabs/audit_log/AuditLogGuildMessages.ts
msgid "{actor} transferred community ownership to {user}"
msgstr "{actor} heeft het community-eigendom overgedragen aan {user}"

#. Activity log summary for a moderator who turned the microphone of a member back on in the voice channels of this community, so others can hear the member again. Describe the effect the way the English does. Do not name the action with a noun such as a community mute, which reads as muting the whole community. The action that lets a member hear others again is a different action and must read clearly differently. This is a past tense record of an action that already happened, never an instruction to the reader. {actor} is the member who turned the microphone back on, shown as a clickable user chip, or the word System. {target} is the member who can be heard again, shown as a clickable user chip.
#: src/features/guild/utils/guild_tabs/audit_log/AuditLogMemberMessages.ts
msgid "{actor} turned {target}'s microphone back on in this community"
msgstr "{actor} heeft de microfoon van {target} in deze community weer ingeschakeld"

#. Activity log summary for a moderator who turned off the microphone of a member in every voice channel of this community, so nobody can hear the member until it is turned back on. Describe the effect the way the English does. Do not name the action with a noun such as a community mute, which reads as muting the whole community and collides with the setting that silences community notifications. The action that stops a member from hearing others is a different action and must read clearly differently. This is a past tense record of an action that already happened, never an instruction to the reader. {actor} is the member who turned the microphone off, shown as a clickable user chip, or the word System. {target} is the member whose microphone was turned off, shown as a clickable user chip.
#: src/features/guild/utils/guild_tabs/audit_log/AuditLogMemberMessages.ts
msgid "{actor} turned off {target}'s microphone in this community"
msgstr "{actor} heeft de microfoon van {target} in deze community uitgeschakeld"

#. Activity log summary for a user whose ban from the community was lifted. A ban is the community ban, not the feature that blocks a user. {actor} is the member who lifted the ban, shown as a clickable user chip, or the word System. {target} is the unbanned user, shown as a clickable user chip.
#: src/features/guild/utils/guild_tabs/audit_log/AuditLogMemberMessages.ts
msgid "{actor} unbanned {target}"
msgstr "{actor} heeft de verbanning van {target} opgeheven"

#. Activity log summary for a message that was unpinned when the channel was not recorded. Unpinned means the message was taken off the pinned messages of its channel. It is the opposite of pinned. The message was not deleted. {actor} is the member who unpinned it, shown as a clickable user chip, or the word System.
#: src/features/guild/utils/guild_tabs/audit_log/AuditLogExpressionMessageMessages.ts
msgid "{actor} unpinned a message"
msgstr "{actor} heeft een bericht losgemaakt"

#. Activity log summary for a message that was unpinned. Unpinned means the message was taken off the pinned messages of the channel. It is the opposite of pinned. The message was not deleted. {actor} is the member who unpinned it, shown as a clickable user chip, or the word System. {channel} is the channel the message is in, shown as a channel name chip, or the deleted-channel label when the channel no longer exists.
#: src/features/guild/utils/guild_tabs/audit_log/AuditLogExpressionMessageMessages.ts
msgid "{actor} unpinned a message in {channel}"
msgstr "{actor} heeft een bericht in {channel} losgemaakt"

#. Activity log summary for a change to a member of the community when several things changed at once, or when the change was not recorded. Each change is listed as a detail line below. {actor} is the member who made the change, shown as a clickable user chip, or the word System. {target} is the member who was changed, shown as a clickable user chip.
#: src/features/guild/utils/guild_tabs/audit_log/AuditLogMemberMessages.ts
msgid "{actor} updated {target}"
msgstr "{actor} heeft {target} bijgewerkt"

#. Activity log summary for a sticker that was edited when the sticker name is not known. The changes are listed as detail lines below it. {actor} is the member who edited it, shown as a clickable user chip, or the word System.
#: src/features/guild/utils/guild_tabs/audit_log/AuditLogExpressionMessageMessages.ts
msgid "{actor} updated a sticker"
msgstr "{actor} heeft een sticker bijgewerkt"

#. Activity log summary for changes to a webhook whose name is not known. The changes are listed as details under it. {actor} is the member who changed the webhook, shown as a clickable user chip, or the word System.
#: src/features/guild/utils/guild_tabs/audit_log/AuditLogInviteWebhookMessages.ts
msgid "{actor} updated a webhook"
msgstr "{actor} heeft een webhook bijgewerkt"

#. Activity log summary for a custom emoji that was edited when neither a change nor the emoji name is known. {actor} is the member who edited it, shown as a clickable user chip, or the word System.
#: src/features/guild/utils/guild_tabs/audit_log/AuditLogExpressionMessageMessages.ts
msgid "{actor} updated an emoji"
msgstr "{actor} heeft een emoji bijgewerkt"

#. Activity log summary when settings of an announcement channel were changed. The changes are listed as detail rows below it. {actor} is the member who made the change, shown as a clickable user chip, or the word System. {channel} is the channel, shown as a channel chip with its name.
#: src/features/guild/utils/guild_tabs/audit_log/AuditLogChannelMessages.ts
msgid "{actor} updated the announcement channel {channel}"
msgstr "{actor} heeft het aankondigingskanaal {channel} bijgewerkt"

#. Activity log summary when settings of a channel category were changed. The changes are listed as detail rows below it. {actor} is the member who made the change, shown as a clickable user chip, or the word System. {channel} is the category, shown as a channel chip with its name.
#: src/features/guild/utils/guild_tabs/audit_log/AuditLogChannelMessages.ts
msgid "{actor} updated the category {channel}"
msgstr "{actor} heeft de categorie {channel} bijgewerkt"

#. Activity log summary when settings of a channel of a type this app version cannot name were changed. The changes are listed as detail rows below it. {actor} is the member who made the change, shown as a clickable user chip, or the word System. {channel} is the channel, shown as a channel chip with its name.
#: src/features/guild/utils/guild_tabs/audit_log/AuditLogChannelMessages.ts
msgid "{actor} updated the channel {channel}"
msgstr "{actor} heeft het kanaal {channel} bijgewerkt"

#. Activity log summary when a member changed community settings. Each change is listed as a detail line under it. {actor} is the member who made the change, shown as a clickable user chip, or the word System.
#: src/features/guild/utils/guild_tabs/audit_log/AuditLogGuildMessages.ts
msgid "{actor} updated the community settings"
msgstr "{actor} heeft de community-instellingen bijgewerkt"

#. Activity log summary for a custom emoji that was edited when no change to show was recorded. {actor} is the member who edited it, shown as a clickable user chip, or the word System. {emoji} is the emoji, shown as its image when it still exists, followed by its name between colons, for example :blobcat:.
#: src/features/guild/utils/guild_tabs/audit_log/AuditLogExpressionMessageMessages.ts
msgid "{actor} updated the emoji {emoji}"
msgstr "{actor} heeft de emoji {emoji} bijgewerkt"

#. Activity log summary when settings of a forum channel were changed. The changes are listed as detail rows below it. {channel} is shown as a channel chip.
#: src/features/guild/utils/guild_tabs/audit_log/AuditLogForumPresentation.ts
msgid "{actor} updated the forum channel {channel}"
msgstr "{actor} heeft het forumkanaal {channel} bijgewerkt"

#. Activity log summary for a change to an invite link. {actor} is the member who changed the invite, shown as a clickable user chip, or the word System. {code} is the invite code, shown as boxed text.
#: src/features/guild/utils/guild_tabs/audit_log/AuditLogInviteWebhookMessages.ts
msgid "{actor} updated the invite {code}"
msgstr "{actor} heeft de uitnodiging {code} bijgewerkt"

#. Activity log summary when settings of a link channel were changed. A link channel is a channel list entry that opens a web address. The changes are listed as detail rows below it. {actor} is the member who made the change, shown as a clickable user chip, or the word System. {channel} is the channel, shown as a channel chip with its name.
#: src/features/guild/utils/guild_tabs/audit_log/AuditLogChannelMessages.ts
msgid "{actor} updated the link channel {channel}"
msgstr "{actor} heeft het linkkanaal {channel} bijgewerkt"

#. Activity log summary when settings of a media channel were changed. The changes are listed as detail rows below it. {channel} is shown as a channel chip.
#: src/features/guild/utils/guild_tabs/audit_log/AuditLogForumPresentation.ts
msgid "{actor} updated the media channel {channel}"
msgstr "{actor} heeft het mediakanaal {channel} bijgewerkt"

#. Activity log summary when the permission override for one member in a channel was changed. The permission changes are listed as detail rows below it. A permission override is a channel-level exception to the permissions of a role or member. It allows or denies chosen permissions in one channel or category only. Use the same word for override as the channel permissions settings, such as Add override. {actor} is the member who made the change, shown as a clickable user chip, or the word System. {user} is the member the override applies to, shown as a clickable user chip. {channel} is the channel, shown as a channel chip with its name.
#: src/features/guild/utils/guild_tabs/audit_log/AuditLogChannelMessages.ts
msgid "{actor} updated the permission override for {user} in {channel}"
msgstr "{actor} heeft de aangepaste toegangsrechten voor {user} in {channel} bijgewerkt"

#. Activity log summary when the permission override for every member of the community in a channel was changed. The permission changes are listed as detail rows below it. A permission override is a channel-level exception to the permissions of a role or member. It allows or denies chosen permissions in one channel or category only. Use the same word for override as the channel permissions settings, such as Add override. Keep @everyone unchanged. It is the name of the role that includes all members. {actor} is the member who made the change, shown as a clickable user chip, or the word System. {channel} is the channel, shown as a channel chip with its name.
#: src/features/guild/utils/guild_tabs/audit_log/AuditLogChannelMessages.ts
msgid "{actor} updated the permission override for @everyone in {channel}"
msgstr "{actor} heeft de aangepaste toegangsrechten voor @everyone in {channel} bijgewerkt"

#. Activity log summary when the permission override for a role in a channel was changed. The permission changes are listed as detail rows below it. A permission override is a channel-level exception to the permissions of a role or member. It allows or denies chosen permissions in one channel or category only. Use the same word for override as the channel permissions settings, such as Add override. {actor} is the member who made the change, shown as a clickable user chip, or the word System. {role} is the role, shown as a role chip with its name. {channel} is the channel, shown as a channel chip with its name.
#: src/features/guild/utils/guild_tabs/audit_log/AuditLogChannelMessages.ts
msgid "{actor} updated the permission override for the role {role} in {channel}"
msgstr "{actor} heeft de aangepaste toegangsrechten voor de rol {role} in {channel} bijgewerkt"

#. Activity log summary for a role that was edited. The changes are listed below it as detail lines when they are known. {actor} is the member who edited it, shown as a clickable user chip, or the word System. {role} is the role, shown in bold with its name, @everyone for the default role every member has, or deleted-role when its name is unknown. The app adds the bold, so do not add ** or <b>. Use the same word for role as the rest of the app.
#: src/features/guild/utils/guild_tabs/audit_log/AuditLogRoleMessages.ts
msgid "{actor} updated the role {role}"
msgstr "{actor} heeft de rol {role} bijgewerkt"

#. Activity log summary for a change to the roles of a member when several roles changed at once or the changed role was not recorded. Each role that changed is listed as a detail line below. {actor} is the member who changed the roles, shown as a clickable user chip, or the word System. {target} is the member whose roles changed, shown as a clickable user chip.
